Z||000000||FTF Engineering||09-16-2001||08:44 PM||||Who recovers leather steering wheels?<BR>Mr.Mike says he doesn't do this anymore so that won't work.<P>The Fiero Store sells new GT like leather wheels that are apparently pretty nice, but that won't work for me because I've modified my core and need to have THIS core recovered.<P>Loki, A few months ago you mentioned <A HREF="http://www.americanstitches.com." TARGET=_blank>http://www.americanstitches.com.</A>  Did you try them and if so, how did it turn out?<P>What other options have people tried?<P>-Bruce (FTF Engineering)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||grgoyl86||09-17-2001||08:01 AM||||Mr. Mike was actually sending them out. Did you happen to ask him where he sent them? Maybe you cna go direct. I understand it was one of the top people doing them for the Corvette folks.<P>BTW, there is another source - try Corvette people.<P><P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Schlag</B><BR><I>Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association</I><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ani_interior.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FTF Engineering||09-17-2001||10:14 PM||||Thanks for the info Bob.<P>Speaking of the Corvette people, there was a tech article on your MAFOA site: <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/steering_wheels.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieropride.com/steering_wheels.htm</A>  that listed a few leads such as:<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>From MAFOA web site:<BR><B> A fellow named Chuck Gaines (541-388-5407) will re-wrap your leather for $150, or install new leather for $200. Highly recommended by the Corvette folks is Barb Pelton (248-681-4336), but her turnaround may be several months. On occasion, Mr. Mikes (800-924-8858) has done wheels for those purchasing his leather interior package, even though he doesn't advertise leather wheels. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Tom Derr wrote that article, right?<P>I talked to Mr.Mike and he told me that he doesn't do the wheels anymore, but I didn't know he sent them out to have them done. I'll ask if he can provide contact info.<P>Let's see... What else. I heard back from Loki... he never contacted <A HREF="http://www.americanstitches.com." TARGET=_blank>http://www.americanstitches.com.</A> <P>I also tried to send a message to David Gamache (from this forum) at reesej11@gte.net and my message was returned as undeliverable...<P>Anyone got a better address for David G?<P>This CAN'T be this hard!!!<P>-Bruce (FTF Engineering)||||reg||1
